cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the deposit below, the thesis, and the article in the references."
title: "Bayesian calibration of a biology-based mathematical model using [89Zr]-CD8 PET imaging and tumor volume changes to characterize therapeutic response to radiation and immunotherapy in triple-negative breast cancer (code and data)"
type: software
license: MIT
# doi: filled in when the Zenodo record is published
# repository-code: "https://github.com/g-rodrigues2/tnbc-cd8-pet-bayesian-calibration"
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues
    given-names: Guilherme
    affiliation: "São Paulo State University (UNESP), Institute of Biosciences, Botucatu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7113-8937"
abstract: >-
  Code and data of Chapter 4 of the doctoral thesis: sequential Bayesian calibration, model selection and
  predictive validation of ordinary differential equation models of triple-negative breast cancer in 4T1
  and RR-4T1 murine tumors under radiotherapy, immunotherapy and their combination, including the
  incorporation of the standardized uptake value of [89Zr]-CD8 PET into the immune-mediated lysis term
  and its leave-one-out predictive assessment.
keywords:
  - mathematical oncology
  - triple-negative breast cancer
  - radiotherapy
  - immunotherapy
  - Bayesian calibration
  - model selection
  - immunoPET
  - leave-one-out cross-validation
